ABOUT THE RESTAURANT
-------------------------------------------

Tindimenu Restaurant is a casual dining space established in 2014 with a strong focus on homemade flavors, small-batch cooking, and fresh daily ingredients. 
The purpose of the restaurant is to deliver traditional Indian meals with a modern presentation style, while also ensuring healthy preparation practices. 
We source vegetables every morning from local farmers and avoid artificial colors, synthetic flavor enhancers, and MSG in all recipes. 

Our restaurant seating capacity is 48 people, with additional space for takeaway customers. 
We follow a slow-cooking approach for gravies, chutneys, and sambar to extract maximum flavor from natural ingredients. 
The restaurant is known for its crispy dosas, creamy North Indian gravies, and Indo-Chinese wok dishes prepared fresh to order. 
We also provide personalized menu suggestions based on customer preferences, spice tolerance, and dietary needs.

Operating hours: 11:00 AM to 11:00 PM, all days of the week.  
Peak hours: 1 PM – 3 PM and 7 PM – 10:30 PM.  
Takeaway and home delivery available via website, app, and phone orders.


