 INTERNAL KITCHEN NOTES (TRAINING CONTENT)
-------------------------------------------

The following guidelines are meant exclusively for internal use to maintain consistency and quality across all restaurant dishes.

1. Sambar must be prepared fresh every morning. Leftover sambar from the previous day should not be reused.  
2. Coconut chutney should be prepared every 3 hours to avoid souring, especially during hot weather.  
3. Chinese wok dishes must always be cooked fresh upon receiving the order to retain texture and aroma.  
4. All gravies must be stored in induction warmers maintained at 65–70°C.  
5. Biryani masala proportion: 1.5 grams of masala per 100 grams of rice.  
6. Chef must taste chutney, sambar, and gravies every 4 hours for consistency.  
7. Use only sunflower oil for daily cooking, except for ghee-based items like Ghee Roast and Ghee Idli.  
8. Gluten-free items, including Ragi Dosa and Millet Khichdi, must be prepared on a separate counter.  
9. Paneer for tikkas must be marinated for a minimum of 45 minutes.  
10. Red food color is not permitted in any dish. Natural color comes from tomatoes, beetroot, and Kashmiri chili.  


